FINDINGS:
1. [MINOR] SPEC.md:1489 — the sentence "`abs` of the one decimal an `i128` cannot make positive, `-170141183460469231731687303715884105728`, is a catchable runtime error" is false as written. Every decimal whose *mantissa* is `i128::MIN` is refused, not just the scale-0 value: `Decimal::parse("-17014118346046923173168730371588410572.8")` yields `Decimal { mantissa: i128::MIN, scale: 1 }` (src/decimal.rs:60-122, normalize at 423-432), and `absolute()` calls `checked_abs()` on the mantissa (src/decimal.rs:349-357), so it fails for all scales 0..=18. The code is right; the documentation overstates the boundary. Fix: say "the one `i128` mantissa", or note that any decimal whose mantissa is `i128::MIN`, such as `-17014118346046923173168730371588410572.8`, is refused.

REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 1
